  "id": "strategic_game.strategic_game",
  "title": "Strategic Game In Normal Form",
  "kind": "definition",
  "status": "staged",
  "href": "strategic_game/strategic_game_strategic_game.html",
  "body_html": "<h1>Strategic Game In Normal Form</h1>\n<p>A strategic game in normal form is data\n$$\n  G=(I,(S_i)_{i\\in I},(g_i)_{i\\in I})\n$$\nwhere $I$ is a nonempty finite set of players, each $S_i$ is a nonempty\nstrategy set, and each payoff function is\n$$\n  g_i:\\prod_{j\\in I} S_j \\to \\mathbb R.\n$$\nFor a strategy profile $s=(s_i)_{i\\in I}$, $g_i(s)$ is player $i$'s utility\nfrom the profile.</p>",
